{"agent":"recover-4e","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`at = text.rfind(\"\\n\" + head + \"\\n\")` still treats a fenced `# ddflow brief` line as the anchor because it only searches for the literal string and cannot know whether that line is inside a code fence. When there is no RESUME slice and the real H1 is at the very beginning, a later fenced line becomes the last match: for example, `_under_resume(\"# ddflow brief\\n## Work\\n```text\\n# ddflow brief\\n```\\n\", \"\", \"\", \"## Open workflow choices\\n- pick A\")` inserts the choices block after the opening fence instead of returning `lead + text`. The Open-workflow-choices heading is then inside the code block and is not rendered as a heading, contradicting the helper’s own “fenced `# ddflow brief` must not steal the anchor” contract.","digest":"c3b5a2544c4136b4","family":"deepseek","location":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/brief.py:_under_resume","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/brief.py:_under_resume"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_under_resume` anchors with `text.rfind(\"\\n# ddflow brief\\n\")`, so any later exact heading line wins over the view H1. Given `text = \"## Resume\\nstale\\n# ddflow brief\\n## Work\\n```text\\n# ddflow brief\\n```\\n\"` and a non-empty choices/reports lead, the match inside the fence is last, and the lead is spliced into the fence (`## Work\\n```text\\n` + lead + `# ddflow brief\\n````) instead of immediately before the view H1. The new test only covers a fence above the H1; a quote after it (normal in Work notes) hides Open workflow choices inside a code block.","digest":"6867ff6e3aa8ee4a","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/brief.py:313","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/brief.py:313"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new fence detector only toggles on `line.lstrip().startswith(\"```\")`, so Markdown code fences delimited by `~~~` are ignored. Those are valid fenced code blocks, so a tilde-fenced `# ddflow brief` below the view H1 still steals the anchor. For example, `_under_resume(\"## Resume\\n# ddflow brief\\n## Work\\n~~~text\\n# ddflow brief\\n~~~\\n\", \"\", \"\", \"## Open workflow choices\\n- pick A\")` returns `\"## Resume\\n# ddflow brief\\n## Work\\n~~~text\\n## Open workflow choices\\n- pick A\\n# ddflow brief\\n~~~\\n\"`, splicing the choices block inside the tilde code fence instead of before the view H1.","digest":"8118006beb689d7f","family":"deepseek","location":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/brief.py:_last_heading_line","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/brief.py:_last_heading_line"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_last_heading_line` toggles on any `lstrip().startswith(\"```\")` and never counts fence length, so a longer fence that contains a shorter backtick line is treated as closed and the next `# ddflow brief` becomes the anchor. Given `text = \"## Resume\\n# ddflow brief\\n## Work\\n````markdown\\n```\\n# ddflow brief\\n````\\n\"` and a non-empty choices lead, the match inside the Work fence is last and the lead is spliced into that fence (after the inner ` ```\\n`) instead of before the view H1, which is the same hidden-choices failure the new test claims to close. The same toggle also hides a real H1 that follows an unclosed fence: `_under_resume(\"## Resume\\n```text\\npartial\\n# ddflow brief\\n## Work\\n\", \"\", \"\", \"## Open workflow choices\\n- pick A\")` returns the choices block first, so the brief no longer opens with RESUME.","digest":"60658aa62dad88ab","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/brief.py:_last_heading_line","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/brief.py:_last_heading_line"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":2,"delta_from":"5d8f8c11ae19dc3a81b7149bdfbcefe438dffb9b","delta_raised":["8118006beb689d7f","60658aa62dad88ab"],"delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":4517,"diff_sha":"ec0663505a5972b00bf33e0a85d7f6d66ef012663bba44267969de05255a08f6","diff_source":"delta review of 1 commit since 5d8f8c11ae","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":8.5,"family":"deepseek","findings":4,"full_coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"70c4c12e2c90055d","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-brief-choices-above-resume.critic.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261108T122440Z-19c4e6cd.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"69279550c1cc72ad4aca069134a94eb913699177","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/lifecycle/brief.py":"100644 4955fd87876083f9f7d646313f72f11276d9f5a8","tests/test_session_start_resume.py":"100644 172bba54aac8f288c7f6b23fdc2b4af29d5c6dbe"},"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","reviewer_digest":"dd08c1466c2b8632","reviewer_families":["deepseek","google","xai"],"rounds":5,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/api/lifecycle/brief.py:_under_resume","ddflow/api/lifecycle/brief.py:313","ddflow/api/lifecycle/brief.py:_last_heading_line","ddflow/api/lifecycle/brief.py:_last_heading_line"],"tree_sha":"69279550c1cc+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"e68e3215a986072c9a743b264","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":154676,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B-brief-choices-above-resume","ts":"2026-11-08T12:25:46.797095Z"}
